   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In March 2022, the Federation of Yemeni Chambers of Commerce and Industry (FYCCI) adopted a new strategic plan for 2022-23. In doing so, FYCCI reactivated Board meetings and regularized them (inactive since 2017), and consulted industrial committees and leadership of the governorate chambers. 
With the new plan, FYCCI made substantial improvements in its value proposition to governorate chambers by reinforcing its representational and networking role. For example FYCCI improved its training offer for governorate chambers by delivering 15 trainings on organizational management, governance, project design, and service delivery. FYCCI also introduced advisory services, and launched a new communication strategy. Additionally, FYCCI improved its data management capacity by supporting the installation of the Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system in 4 governorate chambers, enabling improved data collection and analysis to design more targeted membership strategies by sector and enterprise status. 
In line with the strategic plan, the Federation invested resources in enhancing the performance of the research department. FYCCI published studies on the role of private sector in the reconstruction processes of Yemen, the impact of the truce on economic performance along with specific sectoral studies. By using these studies in engagements with national authorities and international agencies, FYCCI enhanced its reputation as a relevant actor for economic development. 
In June 2022, FYCCI management revised all staff job descriptions within the secretariat to include specific roles and responsibilities as envisioned in the strategic plan. Based on an improved job description for the Secretary General, FYCCI introduced a competitive process to appoint a new Secretary General in February 2023. The ILO technically supported FYCCI to conduct the relevant consultative process which led to the drafting of the strategic plan. Additionally, the ILO provided technical expertise and capacity development to implement selected areas of the strategic plan. This included support to Secretary General of the FYCCI in redesigning the organigram, defining priority recruitment, redrafting the job descriptions and introducing a management performance system. Furthermore, the ILO supported the redesign of the organization&#x2019;s website and the development of a new communication plan. 
The ILO built the organizational capacity of FYCCI with the support of ITC-ILO. Specifically, an FYCCI advisor attended the XI edition of the Master Training in management of EBMOs in 2022. The participation enabled the advisor to refine the training offer for the governorate chambers. Furthermore, the ILO assisted in adapting the ITC-ILO course material to the Yemen context so it could be used to deliver localized training for the chambers&#x2019; staff. 
The ILO, in collaboration with ITC-ILO, introduced the CRM system in the Federation and selected chambers. The ILO and ITC-ILO supported FYCCI to review the generic database design and to identify specific customization that would be required. Between January and September 2023, five virtual trainings were conducted by the ILO and ITC-ILO on the different CRM modules to develop the technical capacity of all members of the FYCCI secretariat in using the software.
The ILO also provided built the capacity of FYCCI research department staff to enable better management of the research activities, which led to the completion and publication of several studies.</narrative>
   </description>
